 ## Unreleased
 
+### Added
+- `--print-config` prints the merged configuration and the file that set each key.
+
+### Changed
+- Configuration is read once at startup instead of on every use.
+- Configuration is searched in `/run` instead of `/var/run`, as UAPI.6 specifies.
+- A missing configuration is no longer an error: defaults are used.
+- A broken configuration file (unreadable, unparseable or with an invalid value) is reported
+  with its path, and no value from any file is used.
+
+### Fixed
+- A later configuration file that contains a section without a key no longer resets that key,
+  for example `default_mode`.
+
